# ============================================================================
# G-Ecom Database Configuration
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL DEV (this sandbox): absolute path works because the project lives at
#   /home/z/my-project
#
# PRODUCTION (EC2 / your server): the project is usually at a different path
#   (e.g. /G-Ecom). You MUST update DATABASE_URL to point to the real path
#   AND give the app user write access to the db folder + file.
#
#   Example for EC2 (/G-Ecom):
#     DATABASE_URL=file:/G-Ecom/db/custom.db
#
#   Then run (as sudo, from the project root):
#     sudo bash deploy-fix.sh
#
#   The deploy-fix.sh script will auto-detect the path and fix permissions.
#
# NOTE: SQLite needs WRITE access to BOTH the .db file AND the directory
#   that contains it (for -journal / -wal / -shm sidecar files). If writes
#   fail with Prisma "extended_code: 8" (= SQLITE_READONLY), it is ALWAYS
#   a permission/ownership problem, not a code problem.
# ============================================================================
DATABASE_URL=file:/home/z/my-project/db/custom.db
